    "definitions": {
      "short": "the throat (as roughened by swallowing)",
      "usage": "× aloud, mouth, neck, throat.",
      "full": "H1627. garon [ גורן ] Jer 2:25 גורנך Kt see גָּרוֺן . גושׁ ( be hard , compare Arabic be hard , of hands, from toil). גָּרוֺן noun masculine Psa 69:4 neck, throat (connection with above √ dubious; Thes Rob-Ges (compare MV) from גרה in (assumed) sense of גרר of a dragging, scraping sound; compare מְגֵרָה ; yet √ perhaps גרן q. v.; Arabic (sub Frey Lane) front part of neck of camel, etc.) — ׳ג Isa 3:16 ; 58:1 ; suffix גְּרוֺנִי Psa 69:4 ; גְּרוֺנֵךְ Ezek 16:11 + Jer 2:25 Qr (Kt גורנך ); גְּרוֺנָם Psa 115:7 ; 149:6 , גְּרֹנָם 5:10 ; &#8212; throat ; 1 of the visible exterior (front) of throat, neck ג ׳נְטֻו֯וֺת Isa 3:16 outstretched of neck (= with outstretched neck); עַלגְּֿרוֺנֵךְ וְרָבִיד Ezek 41:19 and a chain upon thy neck . 2 throat , as capable of thirst Jer 2:25 ; as organ of speech בְגָרוֺן קְרָא Isa 58:1 (|| קוֺלֶ֑ךָ הָרֵם ), בִּג יֶהְגּוּ ׳לֹא Psa 115:7 ; also בִּגְרוֺנָם אֵל רוֺמֲמוֺת 149:6 high songs to God (be) in their throat ; compare גְּרוֺנִי נִחַר 69:4 my throat is parched (|| בְקָרְאִי יָגַעְתִּי ); so also גְּרֹנָם קֶבֶרמָּֿתוּחַ 5:10 their throat is an opened sepulchre .",
      "rootNote": "or (shortened) גָּרֹן ; from 1641 ; (compare 1621 )",
